  intro: String.raw`<p>A model turns a sentence about rates — <i>"the temperature difference decreases at a rate proportional to itself"</i>, <i>"salt leaves with the outflow"</i>, <i>"growth slows as the food runs out"</i> — into a differential equation. The work is always the same four moves: <b>(1)</b> name the unknown, the time variable and their units; <b>(2)</b> translate the words into the ODE line by line (<b>rate of change = rate in − rate out</b>); <b>(3)</b> solve with a method from Module 15; <b>(4)</b> answer the question asked (a value, a time, a long-run limit) with units. This module covers the standard first-order models of HW3 and HW4, one model per lesson.</p>`,
